From: Marco Paniconi <marpan@google.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:09:30 +0000
Subject: vp8: clear cached resolution on thread restart failure

In vp8_decode(), vp8_peek_si_internal() updates ctx->si.w and ctx->si.h
from the keyframe header before restarting decode threads. If
vp8_decoder_create_threads() or vp8mt_alloc_temp_buffers() fails in the
restart_threads block, the setjmp handler returned VPX_CODEC_ERROR
without clearing ctx->si.w and ctx->si.h.

On subsequent decode calls with a keyframe of the same new dimensions,
resolution_change stayed 0 and frame buffer reallocation was skipped
while temporary multithread row buffers were allocated for the new
width, causing a heap-buffer-overflow in vp8mt_decode_mb_rows().

Clear ctx->si.w and ctx->si.h in the restart_threads error handler so a
full reallocation is triggered on resync.

Added unittest.

Bug: 571147583
Change-Id: Ic16476a531796751017182a1ef726756353f49d1
(cherry picked from commit ed2a5b572f0f62a72d2e483dd3031841f08fb343)

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
test-only test/decode_api_test.cc conflict taken as ours;
vp8/vp8_dx_iface.c hunk merged cleanly.

diff --git a/vp8/vp8_dx_iface.c b/vp8/vp8_dx_iface.c
index 7baf5c9ef2e4d3d9c1fc8ca7afc6694f2b4dd93c..df0f987bd1230e1d02cee156c057d209d3156e1a 100644
--- a/vp8/vp8_dx_iface.c
+++ b/vp8/vp8_dx_iface.c
@@ -332,6 +332,10 @@ static vpx_codec_err_t vp8_decode(vpx_codec_alg_priv_t *ctx,
     VP8_COMMON *const pc = &pbi->common;
     if (setjmp(pbi->common.error.jmp)) {
       pbi->common.error.setjmp = 0;
+      /* on failure clear the cached resolution to ensure a full
+       * reallocation is attempted on resync. */
+      ctx->si.w = 0;
+      ctx->si.h = 0;
       vp8_decoder_remove_threads(pbi);
       vpx_clear_system_state();
       return VPX_CODEC_ERROR;
